{
  "_units": "World units: 1 unit is about 0.4 m. Speeds in units/s, accelerations in units/s^2, angles in radians. spriteSize (optional, default [96, 36]): the side sprite in pixels, for planes too big for the default. pivot is in sprite pixels (plane sprites are drawn at 4 pixels per unit); noseOffset, exhaustOffset and propOffset (optional: where the propeller line is drawn in flight, for twins whose engines are not in the nose) are in world units from the pivot. hardpoints (optional): the bomb stations, each {id, kind crutch|rack|bay, offset (world units from the pivot), group (release order, lowest first), maxKg, and for a bay salvo (bombs per press) and interval (s between bombs)}; a crutch drops one bomb per release, a rack drops all it carries together (a wing pair). loadout: the default bombs, each {hardpoint, weapon, count} (count is also the most that hardpoint takes). loadoutPresets: 2 to 4 named loads for the hangar, each {name, loadout}; the first is the default. armament.guns: the pilot's gun mounts, each {id, weapon, count, synced, options}: count is the standard fit (0 = an empty external mount such as a gondola), options the guns that fit, [{weapon, max (most guns), mountKg (the pod itself), drag (share of the plane's drag it adds)}], by default just the standard weapon up to count. armament.turrets (optional): AI gunners, each a weapon, its mount offset and its arc of fire in the plane's own frame in degrees (0 ahead, 90 up, 180 back). nation: the air force that flies it. wheels (optional): the gear as drawn and stood on, in world units from the pivot: leg top, wheel centre, stowed wheel centre, radius; tail marks the tail wheel. emptyWeight and maxLoad (optional, kg): the plane empty and the most bomb weight it lifts; a bomb's weight is in weapons.json. Without maxLoad the plane's weight has no effect.",
